# Shell scripts must always check out with LF line endings, regardless of a
# contributor's core.autocrlf setting — a CRLF inside a bash script breaks
# `set -o pipefail` and other shell builtins in a way that's hard to diagnose
# from the error alone (Windows checked out backend/scripts/db-push.sh and
# db-studio.sh with CRLF, corrupting `set -euo pipefail` into a garbled
# "invalid option name" error).
*.sh text eol=lf
